        "### Q&A\n",
        "\n",
        "**How does the BlackMambaOS handle skill dependencies?**\n",
        "The system uses a `ProjectGraph` within the `ProjectState` to define a Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG). Each `SkillNode` explicitly lists its dependencies (e.g., `PERFORMANCE_SIMULATION` requiring both `FUNCTIONAL_TESTING` and `SECURITY_AUDIT`). The `_run_builder` scheduler performs topological execution, only triggering skills when all their required dependency nodes have reached a `TERMINATED` state.\n",
        "\n",
        "**What mechanism prevents unauthorized data access between different skills?**\n",
        "The architecture implements a Memory Management Unit (MMU) logic via the `_mmu_translate` method. This creates a \"virtual paged view\" for each process, ensuring a skill only receives the specific artifacts (pages) it is authorized to access in its `memory_space`, rather than the entire global state.\n",
        "\n",
        "**How does the system respond to critical failures or verification errors?**\n",
        "The Guardian was redesigned as an Interrupt Handler that processes three types of signals: `SIG_RETRY` for implementation flaws (resetting a node to `READY`), `SIG_BACKTRACK` for structural flaws (reverting the kernel to the `TASK_PLANNING` phase), and `SIG_PANIC` for fatal errors (halting the system).\n",
